# Database Schema Governance

- Every database structure change must include a migration file in `migrations/`.
- Migrations intended for startup execution must be idempotent (`IF NOT EXISTS`, guarded `DO $$` checks).
- Do not add destructive or legacy migrations (`RESET_DATABASE.sql`, one-off data cleanup SQL) to startup execution lists.
- Keep `go-services/internal/startup/migrate.go` allowlist explicit and ordered; avoid glob/sort execution of all SQL files.
- Reuse `ValidateMigrationFilename` rules when reading migration files from code paths.
- When changing table/column names used by Go services, update both SQL migrations and consuming code together.
